  <section class="section" style="padding-top:0;">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div class="eyebrow">FAQ</div>
        <h2>Common questions</h2>
      </div>
      
      <div class="faq">
        <details open><summary>Do you support enterprise SSO?</summary><p>Yes. AuthKit ships with SAML 2.0, OIDC, and SCIM 2.0 for identity providers including Okta, Azure AD, Google Workspace, and JumpCloud.</p></details>
        <details><summary>How is my data protected?</summary><p>All data is encrypted at rest with AES-256 and in transit with TLS 1.3. We are SOC 2 Type II and ISO 27001 certified, and offer HIPAA BAAs on Enterprise plans.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Can I self-host AuthKit?</summary><p>Yes — a self-hosted deployment is available on the Enterprise plan, including Kubernetes and Docker distributions with air-gapped support.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What frameworks are supported?</summary><p>First-class SDKs for React, Vue, Next.js, Node.js, Python, Go, Ruby, and .NET, plus a REST API and OpenAPI spec for anything else.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Is there a free plan?</summary><p>Yes. The Free plan includes up to 5,000 monthly active users, unlimited passwordless auth, and full email/password support.</p></details>
      </div>
    </div>
